<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --card-hover: #22263a;
    --accent: #4f8cff;
    --accent2: #ff6b6b;
    --accent3: #ffd93d;
    --accent4: #6bcb77;
    --text: #e0e0e0;
    --text-muted: #8a8fa8;
    --border: #2a2e3f;
    --red: #ff4757;
    --orange: #ffa502;
    --green: #2ed573;
    --iran: #8e44ad;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 56px 20px 36px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2)); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero .subtitle { font-size: 1em; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .hero .date-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero .war-day { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent2); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 8px; }
  .hero .build-meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .triplet-badge { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #0e1a1e); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--accent); display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }

  .direction-of-travel { max-width: 900px; margin: 24px auto; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #1a1d27); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 28px; font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.55; }
  .direction-of-travel .label { font-size: 0.72em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .direction-of-travel .body { color: var(--text); }
  .direction-of-travel .body .cite { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move { border-color: var(--border); }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move .body { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }

  .disclaimer { background: #2a1a1a; border: 1px solid #5a2020; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px auto; max-width: 900px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #ffaaaa; }
  .disclaimer strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .section { padding: 30px 0; }
  .section-title { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .section-title .meta { font-size: 0.6em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }

  .forecast-board { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label { font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 14px 0 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .forecast-card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; }
  .forecast-card.cat-diplomacy { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card.cat-military { border-left-color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card.cat-regime { border-left-color: var(--iran); }
  .forecast-card.cat-market { border-left-color: var(--accent3); }
  .forecast-card.cat-domestic { border-left-color: var(--accent4); }
  .forecast-card.cat-humanitarian { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-id { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-category { font-size: 0.7em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-question { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .forecast-card .fc-probrow { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-up { color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-down { color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.no-move { color: var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-horizon { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta-reason { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dd { color: var(--text); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicators { font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 2px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-OBSERVED { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); border-color: var(--green); color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-PARTIAL { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); border-color: var(--orange); color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-CONTRADICTED { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-NOT_OBSERVED { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE { opacity: 0.55; border-left-style: dashed; }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE .fc-question::after { content: ' [OBE]'; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .forecast-empty-slot { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  .delta-narrative p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .delta-narrative p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .delta-narrative p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  .scenario-map { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .prob-bar-container { display: flex; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .prob-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85em; color: #fff; }
  .prob-escalation { background: var(--red); }
  .prob-status { background: var(--orange); }
  .prob-deescalation { background: var(--green); }
  .scenario-line { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .scenario-line strong.label-esc { color: var(--red); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-prot { color: var(--orange); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-desc { color: var(--green); }

  .inside-iran { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .inside-iran p { font-size: 0.93em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .inside-iran p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .iran-media-badges { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .iran-media-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72em; color: var(--iran); }

  .regime-watch { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .regime-watch-meta { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .regime-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .regime-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .regime-row .name { font-weight: 600; }
  .regime-row .p { font-size: 1.4em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--orange); }
  .regime-row .drivers { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); flex-basis: 100%; margin-top: 4px; }

  .sources-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .sources-list li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.88em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .sources-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-tier { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.5px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .source-tier.tier-TIER1 { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid var(--green); }
  .source-tier.tier-OSINT { background: rgba(79, 140, 255, 0.15); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .source-tier.tier-STATE_MEDIA { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); color: var(--orange); border: 1px solid var(--orange); }
  .source-tier.tier-EXPERT { background: rgba(155, 89, 182, 0.15); color: #9b59b6; border: 1px solid #9b59b6; }

  .expert-appendix { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .expert-appendix summary { padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92em; user-select: none; }
  .expert-appendix summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .expert-appendix[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 20px 18px; }
  .expert-quote { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .expert-quote .expert-name { font-weight: 700; color: #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .expert-empty { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  footer { text-align: center; padding: 32px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8em; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 32px; }
  footer .next-update { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero { padding: 36px 16px 24px; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.3; }
    .container { padding: 12px; }
    .direction-of-travel { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 0.95em; }
    .disclaimer { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 12px; font-size: 0.8em; }
    .section-title { font-size: 1.2em; }
    .forecast-card { padding: 14px 16px; }
    .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.5em; }
    .scenario-map, .inside-iran, .regime-watch, .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Forecast board + descriptive delta. Predictions are time-bounded and scored; descriptions are sourced and verb-disciplined.</p>
  <span class="date-badge">May 29, 2026</span>
  <span class="war-day">Day 91</span>
  <div class="build-meta">Published: <span id="pub-ts">2026-05-29</span> &middot; Build <span id="build-id" style="font-family:monospace;opacity:0.6;">v45.2</span></div>
  <div class="triplet-badge">&#9878; Triple-blind: Analyst + Devil's Advocate + Judge &middot; forecast-board v45</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- 1. DIRECTION OF TRAVEL -->
  <div class="direction-of-travel">
    <div class="label">Where this is heading</div>
    <div class="body">
      The forecast board shifted decisively toward a contested diplomatic threshold: <span class="cite">F3</span> (Iran-US deal by June 5) advanced from 25% to 42% as negotiators transmitted agreed text to principals on May 28, while <span class="cite">F2</span> (Netanyahu coalition collapse by October 27) moved from 35% to 72% as the Knesset dissolution bill's 110-0 preliminary reading and June 2 first-reading schedule converted a months-long political pressure vector into a near-term procedural track.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <strong>&#9888; DISCLAIMER:</strong> This analysis relies on open sources (OSINT) and AI-generated assessments. Probabilities are time-bounded forecasts with resolution criteria; track record visible internally until &ge;20 forecasts resolve. Descriptive sections enforce verb discipline — any causal/directional claim must cite a forecast or be marked context-only.
  </div>

  <!-- 2. FORECAST BOARD -->
  <div class="section" id="forecast-board">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Forecast Board
      <span class="meta">7 active &middot; last reasoned 2026-05-29</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="forecast-board">

      <!-- NEAR-TERM (<=72h) -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">NEAR-TERM (&le;72h)</div>

      <!-- F5: netanyahu-early-election-by-june-1 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F5</span>
          <span class="fc-category">domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Netanyahu formally announce an early election date earlier than the mandatory 2026-10-27 date before EOD 2026-06-01?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">15%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">&Delta; &minus;7pp from 22% (2026-05-19)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">&rarr; resolves by 2026-06-01</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Slight downward revision despite dramatic coalition events. Knesset dissolution bill passed preliminary reading 110-0 on May 20; first reading scheduled June 2 — one day after this forecast's June 1 horizon. Resolution criteria requires a formal Knesset dissolution vote or Netanyahu naming an election date — neither is expected before June 1. Judge adopted DA recommendation of p=0.15 given the structural impossibility of the dissolution-bill pathway satisfying resolution criteria within the window.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Netanyahu makes a formal Knesset speech or public announcement naming an election date earlier than 2026-10-27; OR if the Knesset passes a formal dissolution motion. Leaks and media speculation do NOT resolve.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Times of Israel, Haaretz, or Channel 12/13 citing direct Netanyahu statement or official Knesset vote record. Reuters/AP confirmation required for international sources.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Coalition partner threatening dissolution without a formal Knesset vote = NOT resolved. Netanyahu 'considering' elections per aides = NOT resolved.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Netanyahu public statement naming election date before June 1</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Knesset dissolution vote held before June 1</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- N1: mou-trump-signs-by-june-1 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N1</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will US President Donald Trump personally sign (or publicly confirm he has signed) the 60-day ceasefire-extension MOU with Iran before EOD 2026-06-01?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">28%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">&Delta; Initial &middot; 2026-05-29</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">&rarr; resolves by 2026-06-01</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Initial. Negotiators reached a tentative agreement May 28 (Axios, CNN, WashPost, Foreign Policy, Bloomberg). Trump told briefers he needed 'a few days to think it through.' White House called initial leak 'complete fabrication' before softening. Simultaneous US-Iran kinetic exchanges on May 28 create political friction. Iran's Tasnim states text has 'not yet been finalised.' p=0.28 reflects a non-trivial probability of rapid presidential action weighed against the friction of concurrent military exchanges.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Trump personally signs the MOU AND a named White House official confirms publicly; OR if a joint US-Iran statement acknowledges both principals' endorsement before EOD 2026-06-01.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>White House press release or named WH press secretary + Reuters/AP confirmation. OR joint US-Iran communiqué published by both State Dept and Iranian Foreign Ministry.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Verbal Trump statement calling deal 'done' without document confirmation = NOT resolved. Envoy-level announcement without Trump confirmation within 24h = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. If Trump signs but Iran's Supreme Leader office does not confirm within 72h = AMBIGUOUS.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Trump social media post calling deal 'beautiful/done/perfect'</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">White House retracts 'fabrication' denial and schedules press conference</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">New US-Iran military exchange confirmed after May 29</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 7-30 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">7&ndash;30 DAYS</div>

      <!-- F3: iran-us-deal-signed-by-june-5 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F3</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Iran and the US confirm a signed written framework agreement (any named successor to the 14-point MOU) before EOD 2026-06-05?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">42%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-up">&Delta; +17pp from 25% (2026-05-19)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">&rarr; resolves by 2026-06-05</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Significant upward revision. On May 28, Axios, CNN, Washington Post, Foreign Policy, and Bloomberg all reported that US and Iranian negotiators reached a tentative 60-day MOU covering ceasefire extension, phased Hormuz reopening over 60 days, Iranian mine clearance within 30 days, US naval blockade proportional drawdown, and sanctions waivers for Iranian oil. White House initially called the first report a 'complete fabrication' but did not reiterate that denial. Iran's Tasnim stated the text had 'not yet been finalised.' Trump approval and Khamenei office confirmation both absent as of May 29 EOD. p=0.42 confirmed by Judge after DA opposing narrative evaluation (see opposing-narrative.md).</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if a named US administration official AND a named Iranian official publicly confirm a signed written framework; OR if the document text is published by Axios/Reuters/State Dept or Iran MFA with both parties acknowledging authenticity. Verbal 'agreement in principle' does not count.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>At minimum, Reuters AND one of Axios/AP/AFP quoting named US AND Iranian principals (not envoys alone). Official Iranian Foreign Ministry statement or State Dept press release also resolves.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Agreement by envoys only, without principal confirmation (Trump/Pezeshkian) within 72h = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. If Iran signs but Khamenei's office disavows within 72h = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Trump social media post calling deal 'beautiful', 'done', or 'perfect'</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">White House retracts 'fabrication' denial and schedules press conference</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">New US-Iran military exchange confirmed after May 29</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- N2: knesset-dissolution-first-reading-passes -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N2</span>
          <span class="fc-category">domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the Israeli Knesset dissolution bill pass its formal first reading (1st Knesset plenary vote, not preliminary) before EOD 2026-06-07?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">82%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">&Delta; Initial &middot; 2026-05-29</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">&rarr; resolves by 2026-06-07</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Initial. First reading scheduled for Monday June 2 per Haaretz May 27. Preliminary reading passed 110-0; cross-party support documented. Netanyahu is not opposing dissolution — dispute is over election date. Main risk is procedural delay or last-minute coalition maneuver. Judge set p=0.82 reflecting the strong scheduled trajectory against a non-trivial withdrawal risk (split between DA's 0.80 and Analyst's 0.85).</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if the Knesset official record confirms the first reading vote passed by majority, specifically labelled the first of three plenary readings, before EOD June 7. NO if postponed beyond June 7 OR bill withdrawn. AMBIGUOUS if vote occurs but procedurally invalidated by Knesset Legal Advisor.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Knesset official English/Hebrew record; or Haaretz/Times of Israel/Channel 12 citing official Knesset vote count.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Vote on a different dissolution bill = YES if it passes. Procedural vote (not a full plenary reading) = does not resolve. Vote occurs but procedurally invalidated by Knesset Legal Advisor = AMBIGUOUS.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-OBSERVED">Dissolution bill confirmed on Knesset agenda for Monday June 2 (Haaretz, 2026-05-27)</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Netanyahu or Shas attempts to pull or delay bill before Monday June 2</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- F1: hormuz-commercial-shipping-resumed-by-june-10 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-market status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F1</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will at least 50 commercial vessels per day transit the Strait of Hormuz (50%+ of pre-war ~120/day baseline) during any consecutive 7-day window before EOD 2026-06-10?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">31%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">&Delta; &minus;7pp from 38% (2026-05-19)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">&rarr; resolves by 2026-06-10</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Significant downward revision. PortWatch recorded approximately 4 commercial transits/day as of May 28-29 versus a pre-war baseline of ~95-120/day. Iran fired a ballistic missile toward Kuwait (intercepted by US CENTCOM, May 28), and US and Iran traded air strikes at Bandar Abbas on May 28, further deterring insurance reclassification. PGSA toll regime remains active; US Treasury Secretary Bessent threatened sanctions against Oman on May 28 for facilitating PGSA-style tolls. Lloyd's and P&amp;I clubs have not reclassified. The 60-day MOU under negotiation (if signed) would phase Hormuz opening over 60 days — even a deal signed this week would not produce 50+ consecutive-7-day transits before June 10.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Hormuz Strait Monitor (or UNCTAD, or Lloyd's List) reports &ge;50 daily transits averaged over 7 consecutive days within the horizon window. NO if average stays below 50/day for the full horizon window.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Hormuz Strait Monitor (primary), Lloyd's List Intelligence (secondary), UNCTAD Maritime Trade quarterly report (lagging confirmation).</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Dark-fleet-only count, Western insurers still refusing = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. PGSA self-reported numbers excluded. MOU addendum (2026-05-29): signed MOU with traffic still below 50/day on 7-day rolling average before EOD June 10 = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Lloyd's war-risk premium reduced below 1.5% of hull</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Maersk/MSC/Frontline announce return to scheduled Hormuz transit</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 30-90 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30&ndash;90 DAYS</div>

      <!-- N3: hormuz-mou-mine-clearance-30-days -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-market status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N3</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">If the Iran-US MOU is signed, will Iran complete clearance of mines from the Strait of Hormuz within the agreed 30-day window (before EOD 2026-07-05, assuming signature by EOD June 5)?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">38%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">&Delta; Initial &middot; 2026-05-29</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">&rarr; resolves by 2026-07-05 (conditional)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Initial. Conditional on MOU signature. Iran's mine-laying campaign was extensive (600+ tankers trapped inside Gulf per Saudi Aramco CEO, May 11). Mine clearance in an active conflict zone within 30 days is technically demanding. Iran's semi-official Tasnim framed Hormuz controls as 'navigational service fees' — a framing that complicates formal mine-coordinate handover to a neutral party. If MOU never signed: RETIRE-OBE.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if UNCTAD, Lloyd's List Intelligence, or Windward AI confirms no active mines in Strait transit lanes AND at least one major Western shipping insurer publicly states Hormuz mine risk has been 'substantially cleared' before EOD July 5, 2026. NO if 30-day window passes with mines still present. AMBIGUOUS if MOU not signed.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Lloyd's List Intelligence + Windward AI (both required); or UNCTAD quarterly + IMO formal declaration.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Iranian government statement of clearance without independent maritime-sector confirmation = NOT resolved YES. Partial clearance = NO. If MOU never signed = RETIRE-OBE. Mine clearance suspended due to resumed hostilities = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IRGC formal handover of mine coordinates to neutral third party</span>
